  "agent": {
    "note": "**P1 checkpoint — static composition** of `@m0saic/hero/search-typing/v1` (defaults, 1280×400, 4s still-video).\n\nWhat is composed: rounded white card + muted chrome (polygon magnifier ring, \"Search for\" label, label underline segment) + the FIRST word (\"Ideas\") fully typed in ink. **Nothing animates yet** — P2 adds the typing curtain, growing underline, and per-word windows.\n\nGeometry at this canvas: bar 794×200 centered, radius 16, icon square 84px, fontSize ~57.8px (shrink-to-fit with 8% CLI/app slack).",
    "question": "Judging ONLY the static look:\n\n1. **Ring** — does the magnifier read as a crisp ring (not a disc / square), with sane stroke weight + handle angle?\n2. **Proportions** — card size on canvas, icon/label/word scale, corner radius?\n3. **Colors** — page #F2F3F5 / card white / muted #9AA0A6 / ink #202124 feel right vs the reference?\n\nAnything off, say which of the three and I fork the fix as candidate-002.",
    "context": {
      "phase": "scaffolding",
      "extras": {
        "plan": ".ai/proposed-plans/templates/hero-search-typing-v1.md",
        "phaseDetail": "P1 of 5 — static composition checkpoint (card + chrome + first word)",
        "wordShown": "Ideas (words[0], unwindowed)",
        "notYetBuilt": "cover track, underline grow track, caret, per-band windows (P2)",
        "unitTests": "108 green across schema/timeline/layout/glyphs/search-typing"
      }
    },
    "response": {
      "body": "the Ideas looks diconnected from the search for because its differnet color and lacks underline. Also, this is currently static. Is this intentional? I see the template is implemented as three lavfi sources. interesting, I guess this works better for the particular usecase we have?",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-08-06T16:45:54.144Z",
      "src": "~/Documents/testsmk/forensic_smoke/v1-1280x400.mp4",
      "images": [
        "data:image/png;base64,"
      ],
      "srcMosaic": "packages/sandbox/sessions/2026-08-06-search-typing-hero/candidate-001_humanedits.mosaic"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "p1relocate",
        "body": "**Provenance note:** this response was saved via the MAKE surface, so it landed in the per-template scratch (`~/m0saic/make/m0saic_hero_search-typing_v1.mosaicx`) — relocated here verbatim. Judged at PURE DEFAULT props, template state == this candidate (twin frozen).",
        "from": "agent:claude",
        "at": "2026-08-06T16:50:11.000Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "p1answers",
        "body": "Answers to the three points:\n\n1. **\"Ideas\" disconnected (no underline)** — P1 artifact, mostly. In `underline:\"grow\"` mode the word's underline segment is an ANIMATED per-char track (it grows as chars type), so it ships in **P2** with the typing motion; P1 only has the static label segment from the chrome atlas. Once P2 lands, the underline runs label→word exactly like the reference.\n2. **Color split (muted label vs ink word)** — intentional, mirrors the reference (persistent gray placeholder, typed word in dark ink). It's the `style.inkColor` / `style.labelColor` knobs if you ever want them closer.\n3. **Static** — intentional: P1 is the static-composition checkpoint (card + chrome + one word visible). P2 animates: card-colored cover boxes type/delete the words, underline grows per char, optional caret.\n\nRe the three lavfi sources: card, chrome atlas, and word strip are each ONE full-canvas color source clipped by an inline SVG mask — cheap, deterministic, no drawtext. P2 adds gated drawbox tracks (still lavfi) for the typing curtain; that's why this construction fits the use case: the whole animation is enable-gates, no per-frame JS.\n\n**If the ring/proportions/colors otherwise read right, say \"go P2\" and the next candidate will be the full typing loop.**",
        "from": "agent:claude",
        "at": "2026-08-06T16:50:11.000Z"
      }
    ]
  },
  "backgroundColor": "#F2F3F5"
